      "title": "Computing a Probability at a Point"
    },
    "markdown": "Given $X∼\\text{Po}(1.1),$ compute $P(X=3),$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
    "mathAcademyId": "q-130051",
    "preview": true,
    "requiresCalculator": null,
    "solution": "If $X\\sim\\operatorname{Po}(\\lambda)$, then its probability mass function is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{\\lambda^x e^{-\\lambda}}{x!}.\n$$\n\nHere $\\lambda=1.1$, so\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1.1^x e^{-1.1}}{x!}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X=3)&=f(3)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1.1^3e^{-1.1}}{3!}\\\\\n&\\approx 0.0738425664.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounded to four decimal places, the answer is $0.0738$.",
